<title>GERMANY: MAN Roland narrows 1995/96 pre-tax loss.</title>
<headline>MAN Roland narrows 1995/96 pre-tax loss.</headline>
<dateline>OFFENBACH, Germany 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax loss			 83	vs 146 loss</p>
<p>    Group sales				  2,360   up 18 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German printing group is MAN Roland AG, a unit of engineering group MAN AG.</p>
<p>MAN Roland said demand in the printing machinery industry turned unexpectedly weak starting in the late fall of 1995.</p>
<p>MAN said the sales growth was due to the high level of orders in hand for prior years. The group said incoming orders during the last business year fell six percent to 2.23 billion marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
